# **Basic:**
- nPr = n!/(n-r)!
- nCr = n!/(r! * (n-r)!)
- nCr = nCn-r = (n-1)C(r-1) + (n-1)Cr;
- nCn/2 is maximum 
- arrange all objects, some identical: n! / (n1! * n2! * n3! * .... nk!);
---

# **Choose k objects out of n:**
- nPk (order matters, no repetition);
- nCk (order doesn’t matter, no repetition);
- (n+k-1)Cn (order doesn’t matter, with repetition);
- n^k (order matter, with repetition);
---

# **Grid:**
- number of ways to go to (n,m) from (x,y) = (n-x+m-y)C(n-x);
---

# *Binomial Theorem:** 
- (a+b)^n = Σ(nCk)*a^(n-k)*b^k [from k=0,1,..,n];
- Σ(nCk) = 2^n [from k=0,1,..,n];;

